Changed: IBTK::FACPreconditionerStrategy implementations must provide
fillGhostCellsNoCoarse(), which refreshes same-level and physical-boundary
ghosts while preserving coarse-fine interpolation data. Multilevel W- and
F-cycles require a level range starting at zero. V-cycles with presmoothing
support nonzero coarsest levels with initialized caller solution backing storage
on all lower levels; ghost filling may modify the immediately preceding level.
Single-level cycles support nonzero levels without this additional allocation.
